ChangeLog file of Klin (KLone until 4.0.0) - https://github.com/DanielTillett/klin

Klin 4.0.0:
	- KLone is renamed Klin (it is derived from KLone by KoanLogic s.r.l.,
	  whose copyright notices are kept): klind and klin are the daemon and
	  the tool, <klin/...> and klin_conf.h the headers, klin_* and KLIN_*
	  the names, klin_sid the session cookie, KLIN_CIPHER_KEY the cipher
	  key variable and klin/<version> the Server header. The old names
	  still work in 4.x (README, RENAMED FROM KLONE): forwarding <klone/...>
	  headers and klone_conf.h with the old klone_*/KLONE_* names, KLONE_*
	  CMake settings (with a deprecation warning), klone and kloned links
	  on install, and klone_sid, KLONE_CIPHER_KEY, .klone pages (and
	  /index.klone), an embedded /etc/kloned.conf and klone_sess_* session
	  files are read. KLONE_* CMake settings move to the KLIN_* cache
	  entries, so they survive a reconfigure. The Windows service keeps
	  the name kloned. All of it is in cmake/klone_compat.cmake and the
	  lines marked "before KLone was renamed Klin"
	- key manager: the key manager process reads the key file itself, and
	  klind learns only the public key. klind decoded the key and handed
	  it over, and OpenSSL's decoder left copies in freed memory that the
	  workers inherited (two servers sharing a key file, the second with a
	  ca_file); the server tests now cover that configuration
	- TLS settings (doc/TLS): the TLS 1.2 ciphers are Mozilla's
	  "intermediate" list (forward secret key exchange, AEAD only; a new
	  default: old clients with CBC-only or RSA key exchange are refused),
	  in the server's order; renegotiation is refused; session ticket keys
	  change every tls_ticket_key_lifetime (12 hours; 0: no tickets),
	  derived from a secret drawn before the workers fork, so every worker
	  takes every other's tickets; tls_min_version (1.2 or 1.3),
	  tls_ciphers and tls_ciphersuites; mutual TLS (verify_mode, ca_file)
	  documented and tested; no OCSP stapling
	- session hardening (doc/SESSIONS): a session id a client sends that
	  names no stored session is no longer taken on (session fixation;
	  file sessions no longer create a file for it);
	  session_regenerate_id() gives a new id at login or a change of
	  privilege; an absolute timeout, absolute_timeout (default 8 hours,
	  0 turns it off; a new default), next to the idle one (max_age, now
	  also idle_timeout; both take minutes or "Ns" seconds); client-side
	  sessions are sealed with AES-256-GCM through klin/crypto.h
	  (kc_aead_seal/open), binding the data to the session id and time
	  (the CBC+HMAC format is still read in 4.x, removed in 5.0);
	  session_csrf_token() and session_csrf_check() for CSRF tokens. An
	  expired session no longer stops the request from starting a new one
	- fuzzing and static analysis (doc/FUZZING): a libFuzzer target per
	  parser in fuzz/ (request, multipart, header, url, json, ws, digest,
	  session, translate), with seeds and dictionaries, built with
	  -DKLIN_FUZZ=ON and run under ASan and UBSan by test/run_fuzz.py in
	  CI; ClusterFuzzLite (.clusterfuzzlite/) on every pull request and in
	  a daily batch with corpus pruning and coverage, the corpus kept in
	  the cflite-corpus branch; CodeQL, clang-tidy, and a Coverity Scan
	  workflow that waits for a COVERITY_SCAN_TOKEN secret
	- fixed, found by fuzzing: a WebSocket worker crashed on an empty
	  first message; LibU's base64 decoder read out of its table on bytes
	  over 0x7f and wrote up to 2 bytes past its output (Basic
	  credentials, WebSocket keys and password hashes now go through
	  klin_b64_decode(), which checks the input first: unpadded base64 is
	  refused); a session variable whose key did not decrypt leaked; the
	  io drivers were called through pointers of another function type; a
	  JSON -0 did not round-trip
	- request limits and request smuggling (doc/LIMITS). New defaults, each
	  configurable: at most 100 header fields (was 256), 8192 bytes a
	  field and 32 KB a header (was 64 KB), answered 431 (was 400); a
	  request line over 8 KB is 414; post_maxsize (5 MB) now limits the
	  body of every method, CGI uploads included (413); max_conn_per_ip
	  32 connections at once from one address (0: off), closed when
	  accepted; max_streams 100 SSE/WebSocket connections at once per
	  server (0: off), beyond which sse_start()/ws_accept() answer 503.
	  Header field names must be tokens right before the colon, values
	  free of control characters (400). Transfer-Encoding is 501 (it was
	  400), and 400 with a Content-Length. A refused request is answered
	  before the connection is closed (lingering close, plain HTTP)
	- a hardened systemd unit, contrib/systemd/klind.service (doc/SYSTEMD):
	  klind starts as root only to bind, chroot and drop, under a reduced
	  capability set, ProtectSystem=strict, a system call filter and the
	  other systemd protections (systemd-analyze security: 2.4, "OK");
	  test/run_systemd_test.py runs klind under it (CI, with sudo). The
	  refusal to keep root credentials without 'allow_root yes' (uid and
	  gid are both needed; a chroot alone is not enough) is now tested
	- compiler and linker hardening (doc/HARDENING), on by default
	  (KLIN_HARDENING=OFF turns it off): _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3 in release
	  builds, -fstack-clash-protection, -fcf-protection (x86) or
	  -mbranch-protection=standard (ARM64), -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero,
	  -Werror=format-security, PIE with -z relro -z now -z noexecstack;
	  --dynamicbase/--nxcompat/--high-entropy-va on MinGW; MSVC
	  equivalents. A build check reads klind's ELF headers to prove them
	- cryptography behind one interface (doc/CRYPTO): klin/crypto.h (kc_*:
	  digests, HMAC, PBKDF2, random bytes, constant-time compare, wiping,
	  AES-256-CBC) implemented in src/libutils/crypto.c; TLS through an
	  opaque tls_ctx_t. Only that file and the TLS layer call OpenSSL (a
	  build check enforces it), and Klin's code builds with
	  OPENSSL_NO_DEPRECATED: SSL_library_init/SSL_load_error_strings
	  replaced by OPENSSL_init_ssl, EVP_add_cipher dropped. Behaviour,
	  configuration, sessions and encrypted pages are unchanged. API:
	  codec_cipher_create() and u_cipher_encrypt/decrypt() take
	  KC_AES_256_CBC, tls_load_init_ctx() returns tls_ctx_t *, Klin's
	  headers no longer include OpenSSL's. Decision: OpenSSL stays the only
	  backend; mbedTLS (Apache 2.0), not wolfSSL, if a device ever needs
	  another
	- native Windows: builds with MinGW-w64 (MSYS2 UCRT64) and serves HTTP
	  and HTTPS in the single-process model. LibU's own stand-ins for
	  setenv, mkstemps and fnmatch are declared and used, its daemon.c is
	  left out; Winsock 2 and a POSIX regex library (libsystre) are linked;
	  TLS sockets are closed with closesocket(); key_manager defaults to
	  no. CI builds it on every push, serves pages over HTTP and HTTPS
	  (test/run_windows_smoke.py) and runs the regression suite
	- sandbox (doc/SANDBOX), on by default (sandbox no turns it off):
	  workers, after the child_init hook, and the TLS key manager run
	  under a seccomp-bpf filter with no_new_privs on Linux (x86-64,
	  aarch64): the calls serving needs pass, ptrace, mount, setuid,
	  module loading, bpf, namespaces and the like kill the process, any
	  other call fails with EPERM. CGI servers also allow fork/exec;
	  sandbox_allow adds calls from a known list. OpenBSD: pledge
	  (untested). A page that made unusual system calls may need
	  sandbox_allow or sandbox no
	- TLS key manager (doc/KEYMGR), on by default (key_manager no turns it
	  off): the private key goes to a separate process before any worker
	  is forked and klind wipes its copy; workers hold a proxy key (an
	  OpenSSL 3 provider, klin-keyproxy) whose signatures the key manager
	  makes. RSA (PKCS #1, PSS) and EC keys. TLS 1.2 RSA key exchange is
	  turned off with it. klind stops if a key manager exits. Key and
	  certificate files are read into secure memory. The server tests
	  scan every klind process's memory for the key
	- request validation (doc/VALIDATE): named validators (anchored POSIX
	  regex, int range, length range, enum) and "params" blocks per path
	  and method naming each parameter's source (query, form, route,
	  header), validator and whether it is required. Invalid or missing
	  required values get 400 (or are dropped); unnamed arguments are
	  dropped (or refused); a value hiding a NUL never passes. Checked
	  before the page, after routing; bad configurations stop klind.
	  request_parse_data() now runs once per request; request_del_arg(),
	  request_get_route_params()
	- IP access control (doc/ACCESS): an "access" block of rules, each
	  for some paths or all, with allow and deny lines of IPv4/IPv6
	  addresses, networks and "all"; the first rule for the path decides
	  (403). A client the first all-paths rule denies is dropped when the
	  connection is accepted, before TLS. Bad entries stop klind at
	  startup
	- HTTP authentication (doc/AUTH): Basic and Digest (SHA-256, MD5 only
	  where a realm allows it) in per-path realms with roles, set in a
	  vhost's "auth" block. Passwords are stored as PBKDF2-SHA256 and Digest
	  hashes made by the new klin -c passwd; plaintext passwords, and Basic
	  over plain HTTP, stop klind at startup. Digest nonces are signed and
	  expire (stale=true). Pages read the user with request_get_auth_user(),
	  CGIs with REMOTE_USER; request_get_method_name() is new
	- security headers (doc/HEADERS), on by default for every response:
	  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN,
	  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin and, over HTTPS,
	  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; Content-Security-Policy
	  when configured. Each is set or turned off in a vhost's
	  "security_headers" block. A site framed by another origin needs
	  x_frame_options no
	- embedded files: a strong ETag computed when the site is built (MD5 of
	  the source file; the deflated representation sent as stored has its
	  own), If-None-Match (304, taking precedence over If-Modified-Since),
	  and single byte ranges (Range, If-Range; 206, or 416 with
	  Content-Range: bytes */size); several ranges get the whole file. A
	  file stored compressed is cut after it is uncompressed. Encrypted
	  files get no ETag (it would let anyone test a guess of the content).
	  New status codes 206 and 416
	- send_enc_deflate: embedded files are now compressed in zlib format,
	  which is what "Content-Encoding: deflate" means in HTTP (RFC 9110
	  8.4.1.2); they used to be sent as raw deflate data, which strict
	  clients reject. Files translated by an older klin (raw data) are
	  still served, uncompressed. Client sessions and compressed page
	  blocks keep their raw format (codec ZLIB_* modes are new)
	- Server-Sent Events (doc/SSE, <klin/sse.h>): sse_start(), sse_send()
	  (multi-line data), sse_comment(), sse_retry(), sse_last_event_id()
	  and sse_wait(), which polls the client socket (to see it close), a
	  descriptor of the page's and the timer. Built on a new streaming
	  response mode, response_set_streaming(): the header goes out with
	  the first write and each io_flush() reaches the client (chunked on
	  HTTP/1.1). Writes the client does not take in 30 s close the
	  connection. Also io_get_fd()
	- WebSockets (RFC 6455, doc/WEBSOCKET, <klin/ws.h>): ws_accept()
	  (handshake, subprotocol choice; another site's Origin is refused
	  unless WS_ANY_ORIGIN), ws_wait() (poll(2) on the client, a
	  descriptor of the page's and the timer), ws_recv() (fragmented
	  messages, pings answered, the close handshake, UTF-8 checked, 1 MB
	  limit by default), ws_send(), ws_ping(), ws_close(). Protocol errors
	  close with 1002, 1007 or 1009; a frame must be read or written within
	  30 s. Also io_pending(), response_set_header_sent(), status codes
	  101 and 426
	- REST routes (doc/ROUTES): a "routes" block maps methods and patterns
	  ({name} segments, a {name*} rest) to pages; parameters through
	  request_get_route_param(); 405 with Allow when only other methods
	  match; bad routes stop klind at startup. PATCH requests. Status
	  codes 405 and 415
	- JSON (doc/JSON, <klin/json.h>): a strict RFC 8259 reader (UTF-8
	  checked, duplicate keys refused, nesting limited to 64) and a
	  streaming writer that checks the structure and escapes for HTML
	  <script> safety. request_get_json() parses a request body (415,
	  413, 400), request_read_body() reads one raw. The fuzz target
	  checks that what the reader accepts writes out and reads back the
	  same
	- timeouts no longer use signals: an alarm (timer.h) runs in ordinary
	  code when it is due and the process waits for a descriptor
	  (timerm_wait(), used by the io drivers while an alarm is set, and
	  server_loop), so callbacks may log and allocate. TLS sockets are
	  non-blocking, so a request that stops in the middle of a TLS record
	  still times out, and the TLS handshake has a 10 s timeout (it had
	  none). The prefork watchdog and the spare-worker idle timeout, which
	  must interrupt any code, use the worker's own setitimer(2) SIGALRM.
	  New: timerm_run(), timerm_armed(), timerm_wait(). Alarm callbacks of
	  user code now run only while klin waits for I/O
	- signals: SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers only set flags, close(2) and
	  _exit(2) (they used to log and free the embedded files); ppc reads
	  and writes loop over partial transfers, and a command goes out in
	  one write(2)
	- fixed (inherited from KLone): ppc log lines read back from the parent
	  were cut to 7 characters; the memory klog stored nothing; a NULL
	  dereference when only a backend has a log; the SIGKILL fallback at
	  shutdown never ran; negative prefork/fork counts became huge; the
	  request hook fired twice on redirects and failed pages; CGI closed
	  its stdin pipe twice and swapped local and peer addresses; a
	  server_list with a leading or doubled blank skipped the servers
	  after it; a failed CGI was left a zombie; a form field leaked when
	  it could not be added
	- translator: page URIs and MIME types are written into the generated
	  C as escaped string literals (a quote or backslash in a name broke
	  the build); dead parser states removed
	- packaging: install writes lib/cmake/Klin/KlinConfig.cmake
	  (find_package(Klin), target Klin::klin) and lib/pkgconfig/klin.pc
	- code: doc/CONVENTIONS (return values, error macros, ownership,
	  process-wide state, signals); header_next_field() and
	  header_count_field(); vhost aliases and index pages are read once;
	  the longest functions (request serving, CGI, server setup and loop,
	  multipart parsing) are split
	- tests: unit tests on the real libraries (ctest -L unit, with
	  KLIN_BUILD_TESTS=ON), the page translator in the fuzz target, CGI,
	  uploads, TLS timeouts, SIGTERM and consumer builds of the installed
	  package; CI runs on every push and pull request
	- vhost: the cached dir_alias/script_alias values and temp_dir are
	  copies owned by the vhost; timer: the clock is read with the alarms
	  blocked, and deleting the earliest alarm sets SIGALRM sooner if the
	  next one is due before it; session_get_cipher_key() no longer frees
	  a variable still in the session on error
	- performance: request header lines are read straight from the
	  connection buffer into a stack buffer and parsed there (no string
	  object per line); header_get_fieldn() goes on from the last field
	  returned, so loops over all fields are no longer quadratic; the
	  timer reads the clock once per change, sets SIGALRM only for a new
	  earliest alarm and leaves it set when an alarm is deleted (an early
	  SIGALRM is harmless: the alarms are set again); the response filter
	  keeps its header buffer when reused; request_t no longer zeroes its
	  512 bytes of address strings; the request filename is copied once.
	  A per-request memory arena was measured and not done: all allocation
	  is ~8% of user time and the zeroing would remain
	- timer: a forked process drops the alarms inherited from its parent
	  (and its SIGALRM, which fork() does not inherit) the first time it
	  sets one; its own alarm could otherwise wait, never set, behind the
	  parent's (e.g. the log flush timer of the kloned parent)
	- performance (profiled with perf on Linux): the timer remembers the
	  process id instead of calling getpid(), a system call, for every
	  request (pthread_atfork() forgets it in a child; glibc and macOS
	  only, elsewhere getpid() is still called); the 8 KB response filter
	  of the last response is reused; the status line and Content-Length
	  are formatted without snprintf(); alias and dir_root paths are joined
	  in one pass instead of u_path_snprintf()
	- performance: header fields keep name and value in one buffer and
	  freed fields are reused (no allocation for the usual request and
	  response fields); a vhost's dir_alias/script_alias list and request
	  limits (idle_timeout, post_timeout, post_maxsize, temp_dir) are read
	  from the configuration once, not for every request; u_uri_normalize()
	  works in place without allocating
	- prefork: a worker started beyond prefork.start_child (e.g. for a
	  burst of clients) exits after waiting prefork.idle_timeout seconds
	  (default 10, 0 = never) for a client, so the pool and its memory
	  shrink back; the pool stayed at its peak size before
	- TLS: SSL_MODE_RELEASE_BUFFERS frees a connection's OpenSSL read and
	  write buffers (~34 KB) while it waits for the next request (~1% CPU
	  per TLS request on macOS). Measured on Linux, a worker's own memory
	  is ~64 KB idle, ~160 KB after plain HTTP and ~400 KB after TLS; summed
	  RSS counts the shared code once per process and overstates the total
	  about 10x. The 64 KB connection write buffer stays: 16 KB cost 10%
	  CPU on a 200 KB chunked dynamic page
	- prefork: the 1 s watchdog that asks for a new worker no longer drops
	  kept-alive connections or retires workers that only wait for the next
	  request. It asks for a new worker once when a request is slow, and
	  every second while a connection is held and other clients wait in the
	  accept queue (otherwise those clients waited until the connection
	  closed). Each new worker does the same, so the pool doubles every
	  second up to max_child: 16 workers reach 256 kept-alive connections in
	  about 4 s, where wrk saw ~50 timeouts and ~30 read errors when each
	  worker asked only once. The retiring worker keeps its listening socket
	  open. New server_watchdog()
	- timer: alarms are timed in milliseconds on a monotonic clock. With
	  whole seconds an alarm could fire almost at once (on any SIGALRM just
	  after the next second started), e.g. closing a kept-alive connection
	  idle for a few milliseconds when keep_alive_timeout is 1
	- performance: 7-15% less CPU per small request (macOS, measured). The
	  timer no longer blocks SIGALRM with two system calls per change (a
	  signal that arrives while the alarm list changes is deferred); request
	  argument, cookie and upload lists are created on first use; header
	  lines are read in blocks, not byte by byte; header field names are
	  copied once; Date and Last-Modified values are formatted once per
	  value; the response filter's buffers are not zeroed
	- performance: the response header is formatted straight into one
	  buffer (new response_format_header()) instead of through two
	  in-memory io_t objects, and an unchanged Content-Length is kept;
	  large response bodies skip the copy into the connection's write
	  buffer (new optional codec passthru() hook, used by the response
	  filter). Measured on macOS: 1 MB responses -18% CPU, 1 KB -5%, TLS
	  -7%; with the change above, 1 KB -15% and dynamic pages -11% overall
	- server: the HTTP backend owns and closes the accepted socket, which
	  was closed twice
	- http: client connections use a 64 KB write buffer (was 4 KB), so large
	  responses go out in large blocks: about 3-4x the throughput for a 1 MB
	  file on macOS; new io_set_write_buffer_size()
	- prefork: refill the backends' worker processes round-robin. A backend
	  at its process limit, or a failed fork(2), stopped the refill of the
	  other backends, which could be left with no workers (no longer
	  accepting connections); prefork.start_child is capped at max_child
	- http: persistent connections (keep-alive) and pipelining for HTTP/1.1
	  and HTTP/1.0 clients; new keep_alive, keep_alive_timeout and
	  keep_alive_max settings. Response bodies are always delimited
	  (Content-Length or chunked coding), HEAD/204/304 responses never carry
	  a body, request body reads stop at the end of the body, and TLS
	  connections end with close_notify. Fixed on the way: HEAD on embedded
	  static files sent nothing, empty pages sent a stray newline, the error
	  page could be appended to a partial response and a CGI "Status:" line
	  was sent to the client
	- build: CMake build (CMake 3.24+) replacing MaKL and GNU make for KLone
	  and LibU; works with Ninja, BSD make or GNU make, tested on Linux and
	  macOS. 'klone -c import' writes autogen.cmake for the site build
	  instead of autogen.mk/autogen.dps
	- removed: MaKL configure and makefiles, skin/ packaging, pkg/, contrib/
	  tools, the RHEL init script, the CyaSSL backend, OpenSSL TLS-PSK and the
	  Kilt URL module, and the LibU 1.x unit tests (covered by the regression
	  suite); the API documentation builds with the CMake 'doc' target
	- access log: fix the timezone offset of half-hour zones (e.g. +1030
	  was logged as +1000)
	- build: no compiler warnings in KLone's code with GCC, Clang and Apple
	  Clang, including -DKLONE_ENABLE_WARNINGS=ON; embfile_t.data and the
	  ppc_write() data argument are now const; kloned no longer uses the
	  deprecated daemon(3)
	- build: build/build.py, a reproducible build-and-test runner with LibU
	  pinned in build/dependencies.json; requires OpenSSL 3
	- tls: port to OpenSSL 3; require TLS 1.2 or newer and disable TLS
	  compression; drop ephemeral 512-bit RSA and the built-in 1024-bit DH
	  group (DH parameters are now chosen automatically unless dh_file is
	  set)
	- session: 128-bit cryptographically random session IDs; client-side
	  session HMAC defaults to SHA-256 via EVP_MAC with constant-time tag
	  comparison and bounds-checked IV and data lengths
	- session: cookies sent with Path=/, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and Secure
	  on TLS connections; new response_set_cookie_ex() with explicit flags
	- http: reject duplicate or overflowing Content-Length, any
	  Transfer-Encoding, invalid field names, control characters, folded
	  or unterminated headers and decoded NULs in URI paths; limit headers
	  to 256 fields, 8192 bytes per line and 65536 bytes in total
	- http: split the query string before URL-decoding the path, so %3F and
	  '+' in paths are preserved
	- utils: capacity-aware u_{url,hex,html,sql}ncpy_s(); fix out-of-bounds
	  reads in URL decoding and substring search, invalid hex handling,
	  undefined behavior in MD5 and path normalization, memory-stream EOF
	  seek and negative read lengths; SQL encoding handles the whole input
	- kloned: SIGCHLD handler no longer touches the server object
	- fix memory leaks at kloned shutdown, in the page translator and in the
	  klone tool
	- test: regression, full-server (single-process and prefork) and
	  parser fuzz tests; CI in release and sanitizer modes
	- tls: force usage of TLSv1+ [CVE-2014-3566 POODLE]
	- webapp: fix background and update copyright
	- reponse: missing response_del_field() declaration in header (patch
	  provided by Mickael Auger)

KLone 3.1.0:
	- *BSD license*
	- Fix timeout initialisation upon select() errors.
	- timerm_reschedule() to reset alarm in signal handler.

KLone 3.0.0:
	- Add IPv6, SCTP, and UNIX IPC support via libu/net.  This change breaks
	  the four following interfaces: request_[gs]et_{local,peer}_addr() which
	  now take and return a constant string instead of a kaddr_t.  Further,
	  the 'addr' directive value syntax has changed in non retro-compatible
	  way -- it's now based on libu/net URIs syntax, e.g.: tcp6://[::1]:8080; 
	  the 'addr.port' and 'addr.type' directives are now suppressed, since 
	  they've been absorbed by the 'addr'; and the 'backlog' directive is 
	  temporarily inhibited (it needs an interface shift in libu/net) and
	  is internally fixed to U_NET_BACKLOG, defaulting to 300.
	- New server loop hook (patch provided by Mickael Auger)
	- Conditional compilation and linking of hooks
	- Fix build when fork(2) is missing, as in uClinux.
	- Fix bug in memory session configuration that prevented use of default
	  values (reported and fixed by Davide Berra).
	- Fix SSL compilation flags missing during cross-compilation.
	- Fix partially uploaded files not cleaned up.
	- Fix bad buffer length in {http,supemb}_is_valid_uri() (reported by
	  Senén de Diego).
	- Multipart/form-data fixes.

KLone 2.4.0:
	- max size estimate of encrypted sessions fixed (session_prv_calc_maxsize)
	- CyaSSL support (HTTPS, resource encryption and client-side sessions)
	- session_set_cipher_key added
	- fix warning caused by missing newline in generated source (reported and 
	  fixed by Mickael Auger)
	- configure: removed redundant parameter from featx doxygen

KLone 2.3.0:
	- Minix 3.8.1 port
	- OpenSolaris+SunStudioExpress port
	- fix a 64-bit platform problem about correct identification of file based
	  sessions
	- fix not-firing timers (reported by Mickael Auger)
	- libu2 merge: use hmap "easy" interface with embfs; integrated JSON
	  encoder/decoder; simplified networking; native BST, priority queue,
	  ring buffer and dynamic arrays.
	- "-c command-line" argument to override configuration
	- apply chroot from configuration under OS_WIN
	- fix minor bug in build (bad clean in makl subdir)
	- exec_page() argument name switched from 'args' to a slightly less 
	  common '_dyp_args' to avoid clash with user local vars
	- fix error page configuration failure on URLs with arguments
	- new emb_list (and emb_list_free) interface to list embfs resources
	- added sample RedHat init script

KLone 2.2.1:
	- fix "can't shift that many" build error on Ubuntu 9 and NetBSD
	- urlencoded variables parsed also when Content-Length == 0 on POSTs
	- added 'temp_dir' configuration variable to override system default temp 
	  directory (L_tmpnam, TMPDIR & friends)
	- added 'klone_sid' configuration variable to override default cookie name
	- HTTPS fix (rollback to http.c:1.64) output io_t dup'd from input io_t
	- added session_get_id() to retrieve a given session id string
	- fix request_get_uploaded_file() prototype (suggested buffer size was
	  wrong and could lead to overruns)
	- added '-n' command line switch to kloned: don't chdir(2) when
	  daemon'izing 

KLone 2.2.0:
	- new url-regex dispatcher (kilt)
	- don't fail on PUT and DELETE requests
	- -fstack-protector-all added by default when supported by the compiler
	- better depencecies check: .d and .kld depend files created (and included)
	  when building (-d switch of klone tool)
	- .kl1 inheritance (new directives: extends, block, endblock, inherit)
	- session init/load/save optimizations

KLone 2.1.1:
	- use session max_age if specified in kloned.conf
	- io_get_until bug fix
	- io_vprintf added
	- contrib/ not built by default
	- bug fix: client request line wasn't properly logged
	- makl and libu resync
	- vars_t now support empty string ("") vars
	- KLONE_CACHE_DIR top-level variable added to cache downloaded files
	- default error page is not printed out if the .kl1 page runs correctly
	  (so the user can set his own error status code from .kl1 pages)

KLone 2.1.0:
	- io_ssl_create client mode support added
	- GET and POST variables can now be accessed indipendently using
	  request_get_{get,post}args and request_get_{get,post}arg functions
	- respawn race fixed
	- response_set_cookie bug fix: s/expire/expires/
	- forward --libs configure argument value to libu build
	- custom error pages response fix
	- kl1 entry functions prefixed with "page_" (.klone page filenames can now
	  start with numbers)
	- added passwd-like authentication (uses libu::pwd)
	- added TLS PSK interface
	- page entry point function fixed to avoid g++ errors 
	- libu sync to export u_pwd module

KLone 2.0.2:
	- bug fix: external libraries were mistakenly found by the ./configure 
	  script in cross compilation environments 

KLone 2.0.1:
	- session_save fix: removing last session var was not possible
	- #line directives fixed in pg_*.c
	- debug hook added in pg_*.c pages
	- minor portability fixes, SA_RESTART check
	- redirects uris ending with /dir to /dir/
	- -p added to save daemon PID to a file
	- vhost impl refactored
	- per-vhost access log support through klog (i.e. syslog, file or in memory)
	- Content-Disposition parser fix
	- Darwin 9 (Leopard) toolchain 
	- Cygwin support added (kloned can run in prefork mode under Cygwin,
	  but you've to install Cygwin on the target machine first)

KLone 2.0.0:
	- virtual hosts support (see etc/kloned-vhost.conf)
	- request_get_client_request, response_get_field and 
	  response_get_field_value  added 
	- index config key added to provide the list of index pages to use when
	  no filename is given (http://site/ or http://site/dir_a/dir_b)
	- per-dir (aka cgi-bin), per-extension (.cgi, .php, etc.) CGI support
	- embfs config file is not loaded if external config file is given (-f file)
	- --enable_fs and --enable_cgi configure args alias added
	- bug fix: sup_fs responses didn't include a valid HTTP header
	- O(1) embfs access via hmap
	- user provided hooks added to get notifies about server startup/stop, 
	  spawn worker children, requests served (--enable_hooks is required)
	- u_{html,url,hex,sql}ncpy() interface changed (return count doesn't include
	  the trailing '\0' anymore)
	- added support for CRLs via 'crl' and 'crl_opts' configuration directives
	- KLONE_TARGET_PATCH_{FILE,URI} and KLONE_HOST_PATCH_{FILE,URI} variables
	  added to provide an easy way to patch Klone source during the build
	- --enable_hooks configure argument added to support user-provided
	  startup/term functions
	- --daemon_name configure argument added to set Klone daemon name
	- --install_daemon_only configure argument added to just install the
	  Klone dameon on 'make install'
	- request, response, session, in and out variables are always in-scope in
	  .kl1 and .klx files
	- CGI support (not on Windows)
	- -Z and -e can be used more then once to provide more then one compress 
	  and/or encrypt file patterns
	- -x argument added to klone tool to avoid importing files that match the 
	  given pattern(s)
	- -F doesn't force iterative mode anymore (use -Fd instead)
	- bug fix: embedded configuration overwrite was broken (libu u_config bug)
	- makl update (ver 1.5.1)
	- libu update (ver 1.1.0)

KLone 1.2.0:
	- bug fix: newline always added after <%! %> C translated code
	- bug fix: posted data can have content-length equal to zero
	- bug fix: unmatched single or double quotes in kl1 blocks no longer cause
	  compilation errors 
	- SA_RESTART used for all signal handlers to avoid EINTR when calling 
	  syscalls from within .kl1 pages
	- more console messages on startup errors
	- makl update (ver 1.3.0)
	- libu update (ver 0.5.0)

KLone 1.1.1:
	- io_is_secure and io_ssl_get_SSL added
	- License update to explicit permit OpenSSL linking
	- request_parse_multipart_chunk fix
	- "Location:" redirect fixed

KLone 1.1.0:
	- cipher IV added to HMAC and to KL1_CLISES_IV cookie
	- makl_target_name used to support MAKL_PLATFORM feature
	- HTTP_STATUS codes moved to http.h
	- klone/os.h code removed (u/libu.h used as a portability layer)
	- response_enable_caching and response_disable_caching added
	- response_del_field added
	- alarm_t renamed to talarm_t to avoid a portability (VxWorks) conflict
	- better startup error reporting
	- children processes die immediately on SIGTERM/SIGINT
	- more standard compliant HTTP response code used
	- REQUEST_URI_MAX_LENGTH and HEADER_MAX_FIELD_COUNT used to avoid 
	  [that type of] DoS
	- better kl1->C translation error reporting
	- minor portability fixes
	- MaKL update (ver. 1.2.0)
	- LibU update (ver. 0.4.0)

KLone 1.0.4:
	- strip target added to kloned (for selective strip when cross compiling)
	- MaKL update (ver. 1.1.1)
	- LibU update (ver. 0.3.2)

KLone 1.0.3:
	- cross compilation support
	- bug fix: bad SSL context free on connection time-out
	- C++ support is optional (--disable_cxx)
	- support LibU minimisation by default: --disable_libu-mini configure arg
	  to compile the full LibU
	- various SSL related updates:
	    - crypto material can be loaded from the host file system too
	    - HTTP/S configuration section added to example-site/kloned.conf
	    - sample server certificate kloned.pem added, 
	    - sample HTTP/S configuration file etc/kloned-https.conf added
	- MaKL update (ver. 1.1.0)
	- LibU update (ver. 0.3.1)

KLone 1.0.2:
	- bug fix: endless reap loop on SIGTERM or SIGINT
	- bug fix: processes handling slow connections didn't term when needed
	- new ports: OpenBSD 3.8, NetBSD 2.0.x, NetBSD 2.1, FreeBSD 6.0
	- MaKL update (ver. 1.0.0)
	- LibU update (ver. 0.3.0)

KLone 1.0.1:
	- first public release

